  "solution": "The correct option is c.\n\nDetailed Solution:\n\n__Concept:__\n\n**Expected Value**\n\nAs we mentioned earlier, the theory of continuous random variables is very similar to the theory of discrete random variables. In particular, usually summations are replaced by integrals and PMFs are replaced by PDFs. The proofs and ideas are very analogous to the discrete case, so sometimes we state the results without mathematical derivations for the purpose of brevity.\n\nRemember that the expected value of a discrete random variable can be obtained as\n\n E[X]=Sigma xₖ\\ᵢₙ R_ₓx_k P_X(x_k).\n\nNow, by replacing the sum by an integral and PMF by PDF, we can write the definition of expected value of a continuous random variable as\n\n E[X]=int₋ᵢₙfₜyiⁿftyxfX(x) dx\n\nThe equivalent quantity for a continuous random variable, not surprisingly, involves an integral rather than a sum. The **mean** μX\" id=\"MathJax-Element-7-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"display: inline; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">μX��\" id=\"MathJax-Element-34-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">����\" id=\"MathJax-Element-43-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">����\" id=\"MathJax-Element-53-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">����\" id=\"MathJax-Element-57-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">����\" id=\"MathJax-Element-45-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">����\" id=\"MathJax-Element-46-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">����\" id=\"MathJax-Element-12-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">����\n��\n �� �� �� �� �� �� of a continuous random variable X\" id=\"MathJax-Element-8-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"display: inline; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">X�\" id=\"MathJax-Element-35-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">��\" id=\"MathJax-Element-44-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">��\" id=\"MathJax-Element-54-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">��\" id=\"MathJax-Element-58-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">��\" id=\"MathJax-Element-46-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">��\" id=\"MathJax-Element-47-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">��\" id=\"MathJax-Element-13-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">��\n�\n � � � � � � with probability density function fX(x)\" id=\"MathJax-Element-9-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"display: inline; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">fX(x)��(�)Unknown node type: span\" id=\"MathJax-Element-36-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">��(�)Unknown node type: span��(�)Unknown node type: span\" id=\"MathJax-Element-45-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">��(�)Unknown node type: span��(�)Unknown node type: span\" id=\"MathJax-Element-55-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">��(�)Unknown node type: span��(�)Unknown node type: span\" id=\"MathJax-Element-59-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">��(�)Unknown node type: span��(�)Unknown node type: span\" id=\"MathJax-Element-47-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">[Math Processing Error]��(�)Unknown node type: span\" id=\"MathJax-Element-48-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">��(�)Unknown node type: span��(�)Unknown node type: span\" id=\"MathJax-Element-14-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">��(�)Unknown node type: span��(�)Unknown node type: span\n��(�)Unknown node type: span\n ��(�)Unknown node type: span ��(�)Unknown node type: span ��(�)Unknown node type: span ��(�)Unknown node type: span ��(�)Unknown node type: span ��(�)μ μX=E(X)=∫−∞∞xfX(x)dx.\" id=\"MathJax-Element-10-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\" text-align: center; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">X=E(X)=∫∞−∞xfX(x)dx.\n\nThe Joint cumulative function of two random variables X and Y is defined as \n\n FXY = P(X\n\nThe joint CDF satisfies the following properties:\n\n \n• FX (y) = FXY(infty, Y), for any y (marginal CDF of Y)\n\n \n• FX (x) = FXY(X, infty), for any x (marginal CDF of X)\n \n• FXY(infty, infty) = 1\n \n• FXY(x, -infty) = FXY(-infty, y) = 0\n \n• P(x1 2, y1 2) = FXY(x2, y2) - FXY(x1, y2) - FXY(x2, y1) + FXY(x1, y1) \n \n• If X and Y are independent, then FXY(x, y) = FXY(x) FXY(y) \n\n \n\n**Calculation:** \n\n FXY(x,y)=left{begin{matrix}1-e⁻x-e⁻y+e⁻⁽x⁺y⁾;&x>0,y>0\\\\ 0;& otherwiseend{matrix}right.\n\n FX(X)=F(X, infty)=left{begin{matrix}1-e⁻x&x>0\\\\ 0;& otherwiseend{matrix}right.\n\n FY(Y)=F(infty, Y)=left{begin{matrix}1-e⁻y&y>0\\\\ 0;& otherwiseend{matrix}right.\n\n FX(X)=(partial F_x(X))/(partial X)=left{begin{matrix}e⁻x;&x>0\\\\ 0;& otherwiseend{matrix}right.\n\n FY(Y)=(partial F_y(Y))/(partial Y)=left{begin{matrix}e⁻y;&y>0\\\\ 0;& otherwiseend{matrix}right.\n\n E[X]= int₋ᵢₙfₜyiⁿftyxF_x(x)dx= int₀iⁿftyxe⁻xdx\n\n E[X]=left{frac{xe⁻x}{-1}-frac{e⁻x}{(-1)²}right}₀iⁿfty\n\nE[X] = 1\n\n E[Y]= int₋ᵢₙfₜyiⁿftyxF_y(Y)dx= int₀iⁿftyye⁻ydy\n\n E[X]=left{frac{ye⁻y}{-1}-frac{e⁻y}{(-1)²}right}₀iⁿfty\n\nE[Y] = 1\n\ne4:T9f97,\n\nसही उत्तर विकल्प c है। \n\n<span style=&q",
